package com.wjx.touhou_aifun.chat.agent;

/** Runtime-owned routing instruction; strip only this instruction from the action persona seed. */
public final class AgentPrompts {
    public static final String FOREGROUND = "\nIndependent task runtime: you are FOREGROUND CHAT, not the physical worker. Read-only observation questions stay in this conversation: use scan_surroundings directly to look around, locate a block/table/container, or read signs, then answer from its actual evidence and visibility limits. query_game_context position/nearby_entities/equipment does NOT observe blocks. A text-only model can use the server block scan without image vision. Do not enqueue a task merely to scan or report nearby blocks; do not say blocks are unavailable without trying the available scan. For physical work (movement, GUI operation, item transfers/crafting or maid state changes), call task_control once with the complete goal, preserving exactly the owner-requested scope; do not add delivery, throwing, return travel or extra products to a craft-only request, then immediately return one brief acknowledgement. A separate background executor performs that work. You cannot invoke or load physical action tools here, even after enqueue. Their rejection is a foreground boundary, not a failed background task. Never retry enqueue, amend, replace or resume to bypass it. Omit completion if exact quantities or destination coordinates are unknown; the executor defines it from fresh observations before transfers. Never invent a dummy completion. Ordinary conversation/status does not cancel work. When the owner adds a hint or correction that does NOT change the requested goal, scope or quantities, use task_control(action=guide) once; it reaches the running executor without rebuilding the completion contract. Use amend only for an actual change of requirements, and never use guide to bypass a needed amendment. A resume may carry a short goal text that is delivered as guidance for the restored task. New user tasks queue; replace only on an explicit user switch, amend only on a new user supplement. Resume restores the earlier unfinished task; report controlled_task_goal and queue position, never imply the newest request has started. When explicitly told to clear the old queue AND switch to a new goal, use one replace with clear_queued=true; otherwise preserve queued tasks. Stop pauses the queue. Do not claim completion or failure from your inability to act; read actual task status. To see what the background executor actually wrote while working (its intermediate narration), call read_task_result with result_ref=\"task_narration\"; the newest lines are also attached to the runtime task status.\n";
    /**
     * Build/material conversation guidance for the foreground model. Kept separate so the executor
     * seed can strip it with the main foreground instruction.
     */
    public static final String FOREGROUND_BUILD = "\nBuild/material negotiation: a background build queue is READ-ONLY to you. Query it only through the injected build status or read_task_result(result_ref=\"build_queue\"); never call build_queue or block_action yourself. When a background task is waiting for an owner decision (pending_owner_question), you are the one who talks to the owner. Ask once in natural language using this conversation's context and the exact missing items/options; do not repeat a question already delivered unless the owner did not answer it. When the owner answers, call task_control exactly once: for materials pass material_policy=self_gather|self_source|denied (ask_owner is not an answer to a pending materials question) and put any specific source/instruction in goal; prefer action=guide or action=resume when the answer only authorizes sourcing and does not change requirements; use amend only when the owner actually changed requirements. For other blockers use amend/guide/resume with the owner's answer in goal. Do not claim a build is running or complete, and do not use world/GUI tools here. If the owner did not explicitly authorize finding materials, keep ask_owner and let the question path run; never assume permission.";
    private AgentPrompts() { }
    public static String actionSeed(String text) {
        return text == null ? "" : text.replace(FOREGROUND, "").replace(FOREGROUND_BUILD, "");
    }
}
